This archive is a Python implementation of sequential recursive least squares
with vanishing process noise \(Q=0\), recorded in:

  Kim, S. Y., and D.-S. Byun, KTide: Sequential Recursive Least-Squares
  Harmonic Analysis of Large-Volume Spatial Time Series, J. Atmos. Oceanic
  Technol., in prep.

It is not MATLAB KTide, not T_TIDE, not UTide, not TIRA, not NEMO
diaharm, and not the adaptive filter of Heemink et al. (1991) or the
RIOPS sliding-window operator of Smith et al. (2021). Those originals
are not included and are not redistributed.

The \(Q=0\) update is recursive least squares (ordinary least squares in
covariance form). Sequential moments (`KSMoments`, `KSPairs`) are not
in this repository; they are at https://github.com/syongkim/ksstats.
Mathematical methods are not copyrighted. This repository claims
copyright only in the new Python expression (MIT License).

Do not cite this software as Heemink \(Q>0\) residual prediction, or as
the 33-name, 30-day RIOPS operator. Those writings are different products.
